<section class="wrap band" id="timeline">
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">The Provision of Information (Contractual Control) (Registered Land) Regulations 2026</p>
      <h2>Four dates. One of them has already passed.</h2>
      <p class="lede">The red line shows where today sits. Everything to its left is already law.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tl rv">
      <div class="prog" id="prog" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div><span class="num">8 Jun 2026</span><strong>Made.</strong><p class="small">The regulations have retrospective reach. A right granted on or after this date must be reported once the service opens, even though the duty itself is not yet in force.</p></div>
      <div class="hot"><span class="num">6 Apr 2027</span><strong>In force.</strong><p class="small">New grants, assignments, written variations and exercises from this date each start a 60-calendar-day clock. Submission is digital, through an individually regulated conveyancer.</p></div>
      <div class="hot"><span class="num">6 Oct 2027</span><strong>Transitional cut-off.</strong><p class="small">Six months after launch. Every in-scope right granted between 8 June 2026 and 5 April 2027 must be on the register by this date.</p></div>
      <div><span class="num">6 Apr 2028</span><strong>Publication.</strong><p class="small">HMLR publishes the contractual control dataset as soon as possible after this date, and at least monthly thereafter. Location, grantee, type, duration, dates.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

