<section class="wrap band mapband" id="dataset">
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">The 2028 dataset</p>
      <h2>What the public will see.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Today a developer can hold an option over a field for years while the title shows only the farmer. From April 2028 the register shows the grantee, the right and how long it runs. Neighbours, rivals and planning authorities will all be reading it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal rv" aria-label="Before and after the register">
      <div class="doc before">
        <p class="dh"><span>Title register extract</span><span>Today</span></p>
        <div class="dr"><span>Title number</span><span>CU 412 887</span></div>
        <div class="dr"><span>Tenure</span><span>Freehold</span></div>
        <div class="dr"><span>Proprietor</span><span>XYZ Farms Limited</span></div>
        <div class="dr"><span>Address</span><span>Land west of Burgh Road, Carlisle</span></div>
        <div class="dr"><span>Charges</span><span>Unilateral notice (UN1) in favour of a party</span></div>
        <p class="dn">A unilateral notice tells you <em>something</em> exists. Not who, not what, not for how long.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
      <div class="doc after">
        <p class="dh"><span>Contractual control dataset</span><span>From Apr 2028</span></p>
        <div class="dr"><span>Where</span><span>CU 412 887, part · 11.5 ha polygon (BNG)</span></div>
        <div class="dr"><span>Who</span><span>Barratt Developments PLC · 00604574</span></div>
        <div class="dr"><span>What</span><span>Option agreement</span></div>
        <div class="dr"><span>How long</span><span>7 years + 2-year extension</span></div>
        <div class="dr"><span>When</span><span>Granted 17 Jul 2027</span></div>
        <div class="dr"><span>Changes</span><span>Assignments, variations, exercise</span></div>
        <p class="dn">Published monthly, free, structured, searchable by location.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="small" style="grid-column:1/-1;margin-top:.5rem">Illustrative extract. Title number, parties and terms are examples.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap band" id="who">
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Who this lands on</p>
      <h2>Four groups, four different problems.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="aud rv">
      <a class="cardlink" href="/professionals/housebuilders/"><span class="who">Grantees</span><h3>Housebuilders and promoters</h3><p>You hold the duty. Every option book becomes a compliance register with 60-day clocks on each grant, assignment and variation. HMLR can refuse to enter a notice or restriction protecting a right that hasn't been reported.</p><p class="need">Needs: a register with clocks.</p><p class="go">Read the housebuilder guide →</p></a>
      <a class="cardlink" href="/professionals/landowners/"><span class="who">Grantors</span><h3>Landowners</h3><p>You'll see what rights developers hold over your neighbours' land, and they'll see yours. Expect firmer negotiation on ransom strips, access and strategic parcels.</p><p class="need">Needs: the map.</p><p class="go">Read the landowner guide →</p></a>
      <a class="cardlink" href="/professionals/conveyancers/"><span class="who">Submitters</span><h3>Conveyancers</h3><p>Only an individually regulated conveyancer can submit. Firms need a process for identifying in-scope grants since 8 June 2026 and feeding the HMLR digital service from April 2027.</p><p class="need">Needs: a clean intake.</p><p class="go">Read the conveyancer guide →</p></a>
      <a class="cardlink" href="/professionals/lenders/"><span class="who">Readers</span><h3>Land buyers and analysts</h3><p>From 2028 there is a monthly, national, structured feed of who controls development land. Competitor land banks, expiring options and site assembly all become visible.</p><p class="need">Needs: the signal, not the feed.</p><p class="go">Read the analyst guide →</p></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap band why" id="why">
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why teams keep paying</p>
      <h2>Not a map of HMLR data. A reason to open it every week.</h2>
      <p class="lede">The raw dataset will be free and every PropTech platform will plot it. LandControl is built around the four things that change what a land team does on Monday morning.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillars">
      <div><span class="n">01</span><h3>Alerts</h3><p>New option in your patch. Assignment to a rival. Variation extending a control period. Right expiring in 24 months with no planning submitted. Each one lands in your inbox the week HMLR publishes it, filtered to the regions and developers you care about.</p><p class="ex">“Barratt took control of 42 acres east of Carlisle. Allocated residential. No application yet.”</p></div>
      <div><span class="n">02</span><h3>Opportunity discovery</h3><p>Sites where control is about to lapse, allocated land nobody has optioned, landowners whose neighbour just signed with a promoter. Scored and ranked, so the first call of the week is the right one.</p><p class="ex">“14 allocated sites, 5 to 30 acres, within 25 miles, control expiring before 2030, no planning.”</p></div>
      <div><span class="n">03</span><h3>Competitor intelligence</h3><p>Pick the housebuilders and promoters you compete with. See their controlled acreage by region, what they added this month, what they let go, and what they are quietly assembling. Grantees resolved to parent groups, so SPVs don’t hide anything.</p><p class="ex">“Persimmon up 210 acres in the North West this quarter. Vistry flat. Three new promoters in Lancashire.”</p></div>
      <div><span class="n">04</span><h3>AI search</h3><p>Ask the question the way a land director would ask it, and get sites, not a filter panel. Every answer cites the HMLR record, the title and the planning history it came from.</p><p class="ex">“Which developers are increasing controlled acreage fastest in Cumbria, and where?”</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hooks">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">For land teams and promoters</p><p class="h">LandControl finds the land opportunities your competitors haven’t found yet.</p></div>
      <div><p class="eyebrow">For corporate buyers, lenders and analysts</p><p class="h">Know where developers are moving before the planning application appears.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap band" id="products">
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Product roadmap</p>
      <h2>What ships, and when.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Register first, because the duty arrives in 2027. Then the intelligence layer on the first monthly release in 2028, with history compounding from day one.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="site rv" aria-label="Example site record">
      <p class="t"><span>Edge of Carlisle</span><small>Example record</small></p>
      <div class="r"><span class="k">Registered owner</span><span>XYZ Farms Ltd</span></div>
      <div class="r"><span class="k">Controlled by</span><span>Barratt Developments PLC</span></div>
      <div class="r"><span class="k">Right</span><span>Option agreement</span></div>
      <div class="r"><span class="k">Granted</span><span>17 Jul 2027</span></div>
      <div class="r"><span class="k">Control period</span><span>7 years, to Jul 2034</span></div>
      <div class="r"><span class="k">Area</span><span>28.4 acres · 11.5 ha</span></div>
      <div class="r"><span class="k">Local plan</span><span>Allocated residential</span></div>
      <div class="r"><span class="k">Planning apps, 1 mile</span><span>14 (3 live)</span></div>
      <div class="r"><span class="k">Est. capacity</span><span>~310 units</span></div>
